  "id": "linux-nvidia-dgx-spark-2x-qwen38-flash-next-sglang",
  "name": "2x DGX Spark Qwen3.8 Flash Next NVFP4 SGLang",
  "version": 14,
  "summary": "On-demand two-Spark SGLang TP=2 Qwen3.8 Flash Next with a measured eight-request continuous-batching envelope, native low-effort reasoning, MTP4 CUDA-graph decode, SM121 QSA guards, NVFP4 KV, native 262K context, and reserved sidecar headroom.",
  "license": { "id": "MIT", "name": "Recipe metadata and launcher" },
  "provenance": {
    "createdBy": "lloom",
    "generatedBy": "manual-curated",
    "source": "Adapted from MiaAI-Lab/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Dual-DGX-Sparks 0f950012c8d8323acac9a08846a32ef7953f5f62 with LLooM-native distributed lifecycle, FP32 recurrent state, a measured-sidecar target, and an eight-request scheduler profile validated on the live two-Spark cluster"
  },
  "links": [
    { "rel": "upstream", "href": "https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Dual-DGX-Sparks/tree/0f950012c8d8323acac9a08846a32ef7953f5f62" },
    { "rel": "comparison", "href": "https://github.com/tonyd2wild/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4-DGX-Spark" },
    { "rel": "model", "href": "https://huggingface.co/RadixArk/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4/tree/7b719225242aacd3dbd3f9407468c2ee9a9d2594" },
    { "rel": "runtime", "href": "https://hub.docker.com/r/lmsysorg/sglang/tags" }
  ],
  "keywords": ["linux", "nvidia", "dgx-spark", "cluster", "qwen3.8", "flash-next", "nvfp4", "sglang", "mtp", "qsa", "sidecars"],
  "capabilities": ["chat", "responses", "anthropic-messages", "streaming", "usage", "tools", "reasoning", "vision", "mtp", "moe", "long-context"],
  "hardware": {
    "family": "NVIDIA DGX Spark / GB10",
    "testedMachine": "Two directly connected DGX Spark systems",
    "notes": [
      "TP=2 runs over the private ConnectX-7 RoCE fabric and starts worker-first under LLooM. NCCL selects the IPv4 RoCE-v2 GID independently on each Spark because the kernel may assign different GID-table indexes to the same fabric address class.",
      "The SM121 packed-varlen QSA kernel, NVFP4-KV layer, and token-id-0 abort/reset guard are pinned to MiaAI-Lab commit 0f950012c8d8323acac9a08846a32ef7953f5f62; all source edits refuse mismatched anchors.",
      "The 627648-token pool still supports two simultaneous native-context working sets; the gateway and SGLang scheduler admit up to eight shorter staggered sessions into one continuous batch instead of queueing them outside the backend.",
      "Eight requests with MTP need up to 32 recurrent paths. The 40-path FP32 cache expands the original 30-path/1.63 GB boot with eight reserve paths.",
      "A live twelve-way staggered canary reached twelve running requests with zero backend queue, but four tail streams developed non-finite verify logits and token-id-0 loops before SGLang asserted a pool leak. Eight is the production cap until the upstream verify path is corrected.",
      "The 0.80 static-memory fraction covers FP32 recurrent state and the NVFP4 token pool while retaining headroom for controlled speculative experiments; 0.76 is insufficient after the FP32 correctness upgrade.",
      "Generic NEXTN renders as EAGLE in this runtime and does not enforce custom thinking-budget processors; MTP and hard graduated budgets are therefore mutually exclusive profiles.",
      "The new SM121 kernel passed upstream exact retrieval at 120K, 190K, and 210K with no token-id-0 output; this LLooM NVFP4-KV combination still requires its own long-context semantic soak before 262K is trusted."
    ]
  },
  "requirements": {
    "platforms": ["linux-arm64"],
    "memoryGb": 96,
    "diskGb": 170,
    "commands": ["docker"],
    "accelerators": ["cuda", "nvidia-gpu", "blackwell", "gb10"],
